---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import ClaimBlock from '../components/ClaimBlock.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const claim = (id: string) => release.claims.find(c => c.id === id);
const premises = claim('C-NSO-PREMISES-2018');
const sufficiency = claim('C-NSO-SUFFICIENCY-2018');
const connections = claim('C-JJM-CONNECTIONS-20260303');
const functionality = claim('C-JJM-FUNCTIONALITY-2024');
---
<Site title="Water and people" description="What India's dated household surveys and tap-connection reports do—and do not—tell us about access.">
  <PageHeader title="A tap is not a water supply" eyebrow="Water and people" description="The distance from a pipe connection to reliable, safe water is measured in quantity, timing, quality and who can reach it." />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell page-grid"><article>
    <p class="eyebrow">The central distinction</p><h2>Access has more than one denominator.</h2><p>A household can have a water facility within its premises, a tap connection on an administrative list, intermittent supply, or water that fails a quality test. These are different conditions. Their datasets span <strong>2018, 2024 and March 2026</strong>; none measures household conditions after the September 2026 rainfall shortfall.</p>
    <div class="story-timeline"><div class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">Household survey · 2018</p><h3>Where the source was</h3><p>In the NSO survey, 58.2% of rural and 80.7% of urban households reported a drinking-water facility within their premises. In the same survey, 87.6% of rural and 90.9% of urban households said their principal source was sufficient throughout the year. The latter is a household report, not a daily flow or quality test. {premises && <a href={url(`/sources/${premises.evidenceIds[0]}/`)}>Survey record ↗</a>}</p></div>
    <div class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">Sampled functionality · 2024</p><h3>What came through the tap</h3><p>A survey in villages already declared covered by Jal Jeevan Mission found that 86.5% of surveyed households with taps had received water in the preceding seven days and 83.6% reported supply on their scheme schedule. Quantity and microbiological results were estimated or tested with different methods; they cannot be combined into a claim that the same share of households had wholly safe service. {functionality && <a href={url(`/sources/${functionality.evidenceIds[0]}/`)}>Assessment and sample limits ↗</a>}</p></div>
    <div class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">Administrative report · 3 March 2026</p><h3>How many connections were recorded</h3><p>States and UTs reported about 15.82 crore of 19.36 crore rural households with tap-water connections in a ministry parliamentary reply. This is a programme count with a different population and method from either survey. {connections && <a href={url(`/sources/${connections.evidenceIds[0]}/`)}>Parliamentary reply ↗</a>}</p></div></div>
    <h2>Who carries the gap?</h2><p>To report unequal exposure we would need local, dated evidence: service hours and quality tests; prices for purchased alternatives; collection time; and which households or workers are affected. The approved national records do not establish those distributions in September 2026. Private storage or purchased water may buffer an interruption, but their use and cost cannot be assumed for a representative household.</p>
    <div class="note"><strong>What could change this answer</strong><p>Matched utility service logs and sampled household observations in named places, with sources, dates, quality, reliability and distributional measures. A rise in connections alone would not establish improvement in all of them.</p></div>
  </article><aside><p class="eyebrow">Continue</p><a href={url('/impacts/')}>Livelihoods and unequal exposure</a><a href={url('/understand/rain-to-tap/')}>From rain to tap</a><a href={url('/states/')}>Find a state or UT</a><a href={url('/data-status/')}>What is unmeasured</a></aside></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Source-linked findings</p><h2>Read the four records</h2><p>These records retain each source's dates, population and limitations. They are not points on one trend line.</p>{premises && <ClaimBlock claim={premises} heading="2018: facility within premises" />}{sufficiency && <ClaimBlock claim={sufficiency} heading="2018: reported year-round sufficiency" />}{functionality && <ClaimBlock claim={functionality} heading="2024: sampled functionality" />}{connections && <ClaimBlock claim={connections} heading="2026: reported connections" />}</div></section>
</Site>
